BAR Droid phone version of BAR's pre-game UI (luaui/widgets/gui_pregameui.lua): its Ready button (Lock / Unlock
position, offer as a substitute) a finger's height, and on the screen. BAR sizes it by its interface scale, 40 high
and words of 24 times it: on the dev phone upright about 48 pixels, 2.5 mm, the button every online game asks to be
tapped (2026-11-19, a skirmish started from the lobby, its start point placed). At least 8.5 % of the screen's short
side now, as the quit dialog's buttons (phone-widget-gui_top_bar_buttons.lua.patch), its words as much larger, moved
left if it would run past the screen's right edge. BAR's interface scale itself stays (the start countdown's place
uses it; bardroid_chat.lua keeps its lines clear of it by BAR's numbers). And its rect for the app's touch widget
(WG.BarDroidTapPanels): a tap on it hides the pointer, a drag from it pans. Applied by the engine (BarDroidPhoneLuaDir)
to BAR's file as LuaUI loads it; if a block finds no place, BAR's own file runs.

@@@ find
local buttonDrawn = false
@@@ with
local buttonDrawn = false
local droidButtonFs -- BAR Droid (phone): the button's words, as large as the button (ViewResize)
@@@ end

@@@ find
	buttonW = mathFloor(orgbuttonW * uiScale / 2) * 2
	buttonH = mathFloor(orgbuttonH * uiScale / 2) * 2

	UiElement = WG.FlowUI.Draw.Element
@@@ with
	-- BAR Droid (phone): a finger's height, at least 8.5 % of the screen's short side (its words with it)
	local droidF = math.max(1, math.min(vsx, vsy) * 0.085 / math.max(1, orgbuttonH * uiScale))
	buttonW = mathFloor(orgbuttonW * uiScale * droidF / 2) * 2
	buttonH = mathFloor(orgbuttonH * uiScale * droidF / 2) * 2
	droidButtonFs = 24 * uiScale * droidF

	UiElement = WG.FlowUI.Draw.Element
@@@ end

@@@ find
	uiPadding = mathFloor(elementPadding * 4.5)

	createButton()
end
@@@ with
	uiPadding = mathFloor(elementPadding * 4.5)
	-- BAR Droid (phone): on the screen whole (larger, a long caption ran past the right edge upright)
	buttonX = math.max(mathFloor(buttonW / 2) + uiPadding, math.min(buttonX, vsx - mathFloor(buttonW / 2) - uiPadding - 2))

	createButton()
end
@@@ end

